This PR introduces a new Terraform resource: `datadog_monitor_notification_rule`, which supports managing [Datadog Monitor Notification Rules](https://docs.datadoghq.com/api/latest/monitors/?code-lang=curl#get-a-monitor-notification-rule).

This resource allows users to define reusable notification rules that can be applied to multiple monitors via tag filters. It simplifies and centralizes notification configuration, reducing the need to manage alert channels individually across many monitors.

#### Example
```
resource "datadog_monitor_notification_rule" "foo" {
  name       = "A notification rule name"
  recipients = ["slack-test-channel", "jira-test"]
  filter {
    tags = ["env:abc"]
  }
}
```

