POC based on this [design doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t3UfbTphJ1oJnvFchf6n-oV8vWwVEXIfwZSQCjhNsCg/edit?tab=t.3igmqzn72kuh#heading=h.vffpys9wixwy)

This PR implements proposal 2 - uses arbitrary string `element_identifier` for element keys while the system internally maintains a mapping to a numeric `panelId` (dual keys). 

Feature toggle to enable: `useV2DashboardsApi`

How? We are creating mapping layer to associate each arbitrary string key with the `panelId`.  A lookup table that looks like this

```
// Format {element_identifier: Paneld}

example:
{
   6 : my-custom-panel,
   7 : another-panel		 
}
```

This numeric identifier is then used by all backend and frontend components that require numbers (for instance, SceneQueryRunner, annotations, alerting, URL generation, and grid layout calculations).
